Fixed and verified.

The bug was in `advanceTurn` at `src/sim.ts:43`. The growth check used `foodSurplus >= 0`, so a settlement exactly at break-even (`foodProduced === foodConsumed`, i.e. `foodSurplus === 0`) still grew population by 1 each turn. Since break-even isn't a surplus, population should not grow there.

Change:
- `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` → `if (foodSurplus > 0)`

Population now grows only on a genuine food surplus. All 4 tests pass and `tsc --noEmit` is clean.


